WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.569 --> 00:00:07.800
- <i>[Gunshot]</i>
- Lieutenant. I received a letter from Tony.

2
00:00:07.873 --> 00:00:10.068
Well. he's perfectly all right.

3
00:00:10.142 --> 00:00:13.475
<i>Really. </i>
How big a ransom
did the letter ask for. ma'am?

4
00:00:13.545 --> 00:00:18.346
I must say. the lieutenant's
investigatory procedures
do differ somewhat from my own.

5
00:00:18.417 --> 00:00:20.408
Well. that speaks very well
for you. Sergeant Wilson.

6
00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:28.074
Watch Online Movies and Series for FREE
www.osdb.link/lm

7
00:00:39.471 --> 00:00:42.304
<i>[Phone Ringing]</i>

8
00:00:48.346 --> 00:00:50.712
<i>[Ringing Continues]</i>

9
00:00:56.755 --> 00:00:58.882
Hello?
[Man]
Mrs. Goodland?

10
00:00:58.957 --> 00:01:01.653
Yes.
Mrs. Tony Goodland?

11
00:01:01.726 --> 00:01:03.956
Who is this?
Never mind.

12
00:01:04.029 --> 00:01:06.623
I just wouldn't go any place
if I was you.

13
00:01:06.698 --> 00:01:08.893
Your old man. he just
bought himself some trouble.

14
00:01:08.967 --> 00:01:11.902
He's what?
What are you talking about?

15
00:01:11.970 --> 00:01:14.461
Just stay put. lady.

16
00:01:14.539 --> 00:01:17.235
If he pays up.
no hard feelings.

17
00:01:17.309 --> 00:01:20.836
If he don't.
we'll be in touch with you.

18
00:01:20.912 --> 00:01:24.143
Get in touch? What is this?

19
00:01:24.216 --> 00:01:27.447
[Line Disconnects]
[Dial Tone Humming]

20
00:01:33.391 --> 00:01:35.382
Tony?

21
00:01:47.272 --> 00:01:49.263
Tony?

22
00:02:20.672 --> 00:02:24.005
[Ringing]

23
00:02:24.075 --> 00:02:27.909
Hello? Whom?

24
00:02:27.979 --> 00:02:30.277
Mrs. Tony Goodland.

25
00:02:30.348 --> 00:02:33.408
And if my husband is there. Miss West.
I'd like to speak with him. please.

26
00:02:33.485 --> 00:02:37.114
Well. why would you...
I mean. what makes you...

27
00:02:37.188 --> 00:02:40.988
I know what you mean. dear.
and you know what I mean.
Now. is he there or isn't he?

28
00:02:41.059 --> 00:02:43.653
Well. he certainly is not.

29
00:02:43.728 --> 00:02:46.390
Now I was at one time Tony's...

30
00:02:46.464 --> 00:02:49.297
Mr. Goodland's receptionist employee.
Mrs. Goodland.

31
00:02:49.367 --> 00:02:51.426
And that is absolutely all!

32
00:02:51.503 --> 00:02:55.496
I know all about
your skills at the office.
Just tell me where Tony is.

33
00:02:55.574 --> 00:02:59.374
Well. I don't know where he is.
Honest. Mrs. Goodland.

34
00:02:59.444 --> 00:03:02.436
[Line Disconnects]
[Dial Tone Humming]

35
00:03:15.694 --> 00:03:18.128
Jarvis?
I'm looking for Tony.

36
00:03:18.196 --> 00:03:21.597
<i>Ah. sweet Catherine. </i>
<i>Looking for Tony. are you? </i>

37
00:03:21.666 --> 00:03:24.226
My. what a pleasant surprise
for him.

38
00:03:24.302 --> 00:03:27.032
Tell me. my dear.
Have you tried your own home?

39
00:03:27.105 --> 00:03:31.132
- I am home.
- Well. a double surprise.

40
00:03:31.209 --> 00:03:35.543
Jarvis. look. I'm not in the mood
for playing badminton right now.

41
00:03:35.614 --> 00:03:38.105
I got a weird phone call
a couple of minutes ago and l...

42
00:03:38.183 --> 00:03:42.051
- Did you? One of your friends?
- Damn it. Jarvis. Will you listen?

43
00:03:44.823 --> 00:03:47.018
Oh.

44
00:03:47.092 --> 00:03:49.253
Sounds quite lethal. doesn't he?

45
00:03:50.929 --> 00:03:53.693
Well. I tell you. Cathy.
why don't you wait an hour.

46
00:03:53.765 --> 00:03:58.896
and ifTony doesn't come weaving
in by then. why don't you call
the authorities.

47
00:03:58.970 --> 00:04:01.939
Yes. of course. the police.

48
00:04:02.007 --> 00:04:05.499
Drunks and errand husbands
are their special province. I believe.

49
00:04:06.878 --> 00:04:10.405
Not at all. my dear.
Oh. and. Cathy.

50
00:04:10.482 --> 00:04:12.916
assuming nothing is wrong
with Tony.

51
00:04:12.984 --> 00:04:16.249
it's been my pleasure
to hear you so upset. my dear.

52
00:04:19.457 --> 00:04:24.360
Torpedoes running straight.
hot and normal.

53
00:04:24.429 --> 00:04:27.489
Why do you always
have to talk to her
like she was some kind of a...

54
00:04:27.565 --> 00:04:31.001
Well. isn't she?
I've told you before.
knock off that stuff.

55
00:04:31.069 --> 00:04:33.867
And the word for you
is still "gullible."

56
00:04:33.938 --> 00:04:36.338
Why do you insist upon
being in love with a wife...

57
00:04:36.408 --> 00:04:39.536
who spends all your cash
on some skiing instructor?

58
00:04:39.611 --> 00:04:41.670
Maybe I've fooled around
a little bit myself.

59
00:04:41.746 --> 00:04:44.579
In self-defense. dear boy.

60
00:04:44.649 --> 00:04:47.880
Of course. you are embarrassingly weak
and far too decent...

61
00:04:47.952 --> 00:04:50.921
to compete with
your Catherine the great.

62
00:04:50.989 --> 00:04:54.516
UncleJarvis. I'm warning you.
I don't want to hear
any more talk about...

63
00:04:58.763 --> 00:05:03.860
Look. this whole thing better work.
It just better work. that's all.

64
00:05:03.935 --> 00:05:06.768
Oh. it'll work.
I planned it.

65
00:05:06.838 --> 00:05:10.467
And now let's be off
to conclude phase one.
shall we. nephew?

66
00:05:10.542 --> 00:05:14.342
Now wait a minute. Wait a minute.
What if Cathy calls
you back again later?

67
00:05:16.347 --> 00:05:18.907
She'll get a busy signal.

68
00:06:09.701 --> 00:06:11.965
I thought I told you
to listen to the police calls.

69
00:06:12.036 --> 00:06:15.369
I have been.
I just turned it off.
Then turn it on again.

70
00:06:16.808 --> 00:06:19.800
[Man Over Radio. Indistinct]

71
00:06:22.313 --> 00:06:25.840
[Woman Over Radio]
Three-car collision at the corner
of Sepulveda and...

72
00:06:25.917 --> 00:06:29.751
<i>[Police Radio Chatter Continues]</i>
Now. what about
tomorrow night?

73
00:06:29.821 --> 00:06:32.688
I make the first phone call to Cathy
between midnight and 12:30.

74
00:06:32.757 --> 00:06:35.453
From?
That roadside phone
just below here.

75
00:06:35.527 --> 00:06:39.691
And the second call?
Twenty minutes later
from the same phone.

76
00:06:39.764 --> 00:06:42.790
To you. at that gas station
on Wilshire.

77
00:06:42.867 --> 00:06:45.335
Good.
Boo.

78
00:06:45.403 --> 00:06:49.100
It's gonna feel like Halloween
wearing this thing.
Well. don't forget to wear these.

79
00:06:49.174 --> 00:06:52.871
We don't want some clod
trying to match footprints.
Now. where's the letter?

80
00:06:52.944 --> 00:06:54.878
Oh. Here.

81
00:06:54.946 --> 00:06:57.471
I copied straight
from your draft.
Word for word?

82
00:06:57.549 --> 00:06:59.915
<i>Yes.! </i>
What about fingerprints?

83
00:06:59.984 --> 00:07:01.918
Only mine on the letter
and the envelope.

84
00:07:01.986 --> 00:07:04.750
[Woman Over Radio]
Anthony Goodland. age 31.
Hey. listen.

85
00:07:04.823 --> 00:07:08.054
Driving yellow sports car.
Chrome-spoke wheels.

86
00:07:08.126 --> 00:07:12.563
<i>License ZZ03 2 4.</i>

87
00:07:12.630 --> 00:07:17.158
<i>All cars. report if subject</i>
<i>is located. </i>
Well. we are in business.

88
00:07:17.235 --> 00:07:20.068
And now. dear nephew.
to phase two.

89
00:07:20.138 --> 00:07:22.072
<i>Listen. Jarvis. </i>

90
00:07:22.140 --> 00:07:25.871
Couldn't we just hide theJag?
That thing cost me a bundle.

91
00:07:25.944 --> 00:07:28.674
Did it cost you $300.000?

92
00:08:01.913 --> 00:08:05.246
Headlights off.
I know.

93
00:08:05.316 --> 00:08:07.716
Dashboard clock set back to 12:18.

94
00:08:11.556 --> 00:08:13.547
<i>Windows up.! </i>

95
00:08:17.328 --> 00:08:19.888
Emergency brake off?
Yes!

96
00:08:19.964 --> 00:08:23.058
- Flaps up. wheels down.
- Would you mind?

97
00:08:34.846 --> 00:08:37.576
Well. don't just stand there.
Push!

98
00:08:44.322 --> 00:08:46.654
Come on!

99
00:09:01.806 --> 00:09:04.468
The end of a perfect day.

100
00:09:14.319 --> 00:09:17.311
<i>[Man Over Radio]</i>
<i>Stand by. Information incomplete. </i>

101
00:09:29.667 --> 00:09:33.330
Hey. mister.
didn't you see me signaling?
I'm a cop. sir.

102
00:09:33.404 --> 00:09:36.100
Right. you're a cop.
Now can you back this up
and move it down the hill?

103
00:09:36.174 --> 00:09:38.768
Officer. you don't understand.
I'm a member of the force.
Lieutenant.

104
00:09:38.843 --> 00:09:41.778
Lieutenant. don't worry
about your car. The officer
will move it for you.

105
00:09:41.846 --> 00:09:44.576
Officer. right now.
A lieutenant?

106
00:09:44.649 --> 00:09:47.777
This way. sir.
Oh. thank you.
Thank you very much.

107
00:09:47.852 --> 00:09:50.184
Thank you very much.

108
00:09:55.226 --> 00:09:57.922
Sir... Oh. sir. may I?

109
00:10:05.136 --> 00:10:07.730
Oh. fine.

110
00:10:07.805 --> 00:10:12.572
Sir. the vehicle's point
of descent is right over there.
You'll notice the skid marks of course.

111
00:10:12.643 --> 00:10:17.205
These are the. uh...
These are the second set
of skid marks here?

112
00:10:17.281 --> 00:10:20.876
No. sir. The second set
is right over here.

113
00:10:20.952 --> 00:10:22.943
It's a bigger. heavier vehicle.

114
00:10:23.021 --> 00:10:26.513
Of course. I don't have to
tell you that. sir.
Oh. please. You could tell me.

115
00:10:26.591 --> 00:10:29.856
Well. the smaller vehicle is the vehicle
that descended into the canyon.

116
00:10:29.927 --> 00:10:32.725
Here. I'll show you
the quickest way down.

117
00:10:57.722 --> 00:11:00.020
<i>Lieutenant? </i>
It's a... little steep.

118
00:11:00.091 --> 00:11:02.855
<i>Yes. sir. Sir? </i>

119
00:11:02.927 --> 00:11:07.057
But I'll tell you.
it was the quickest way down.
<i>Oh. yes. by far. </i>

120
00:11:07.131 --> 00:11:10.123
Here. sir.
[Groans]
Thank you.

121
00:11:17.909 --> 00:11:21.037
[Muttering]
This is the car
right here. sir.

122
00:11:22.547 --> 00:11:25.345
Subject vehicle. a Jaguar.
registered to subject person...

123
00:11:25.416 --> 00:11:28.317
of last night's missing person report.
Anthony Goodland.

124
00:11:28.386 --> 00:11:31.378
Male Caucasian.
residing 11 Hightower Road.

125
00:11:31.456 --> 00:11:36.553
Discovered approximately
one hour ago by two juveniles
taking a shortcut to school.

126
00:11:36.627 --> 00:11:39.790
You want their names. Lieutenant?
What? Who? I'm sorry?

127
00:11:39.864 --> 00:11:42.526
The juveniles. I have their names
right here when you need them.

128
00:11:42.600 --> 00:11:45.194
Yeah. Very good. Very good.
<i>Yes. sir. </i>

129
00:11:45.269 --> 00:11:48.864
Soil moisture tests
beneath subject vehicle...

130
00:11:48.940 --> 00:11:51.670
indicate residual dew.

131
00:11:51.742 --> 00:11:53.801
<i>indicating in turn</i>
<i>that subject vehicle... </i>

132
00:11:53.878 --> 00:11:56.210
has been here since last night.

133
00:11:56.280 --> 00:11:59.545
That is substantiated
by subject vehicle's electric clock...

134
00:11:59.617 --> 00:12:03.109
which stopped running at 12:18.

135
00:12:03.187 --> 00:12:06.645
Bullet hole in window
on driver's side. but no blood.

136
00:12:06.724 --> 00:12:09.192
indicating preliminarily
that bullet missed.

137
00:12:09.260 --> 00:12:11.751
Bullet slug lodged
in back of passenger seat.

138
00:12:11.829 --> 00:12:15.196
Lights. ignition.
emergency brake. all off.
[Chuckles]

139
00:12:15.266 --> 00:12:19.566
Well. sir. I guess I don't have to tell you
what this all adds up to.

140
00:12:19.637 --> 00:12:22.868
Adds up to?
Yes. you can tell me.

141
00:12:22.940 --> 00:12:26.774
As I reconstruct it. sir.
Mr. Goodland was halted...

142
00:12:26.844 --> 00:12:28.869
by the shot you
were looking at there.

143
00:12:28.946 --> 00:12:31.574
forced out of the car.
which was then pushed over the side.

144
00:12:31.649 --> 00:12:35.312
This to conceal the fact
that he was grabbed by a person
or persons unknown.

145
00:12:35.386 --> 00:12:37.616
That jibe with your thinking. sir?

146
00:12:37.688 --> 00:12:41.818
Uh. I was wondering.
Could you tell me your name?

147
00:12:41.893 --> 00:12:45.556
Oh. I'm terribly sorry. sir.
Detective Sergeant Frederic Wilson.

148
00:12:45.630 --> 00:12:49.532
Sir. please. forgive my rudeness.
Oh. no. that's perfectly all right.

149
00:12:49.600 --> 00:12:53.195
One years experience Homicide.
two years Advanced Police School.
Berkeley.

150
00:12:53.271 --> 00:12:56.104
returned to city Homicide.
six July.

151
00:12:56.174 --> 00:12:59.871
Wow. Well. you're a very
efficient officer. I can see that.
Thank you. sir.

152
00:12:59.944 --> 00:13:03.505
With permission from Captain Ritchie
to work right alongside you. sir.

153
00:13:05.616 --> 00:13:07.550
You're gonna work
along with me?

154
00:13:07.618 --> 00:13:10.416
l. uh. do hope
that's acceptable to you. sir.

155
00:13:10.488 --> 00:13:15.790
Uh. Captain Ritchie did say you were fast
becoming a legend in the department.

156
00:13:18.896 --> 00:13:21.126
Oh. Captain Ritchie said that?
Oh. yes. indeed.

157
00:13:21.199 --> 00:13:25.693
Oh. Well. Do you have
a pocketknife?

158
00:13:25.770 --> 00:13:28.034
Yes. sir.

159
00:13:30.007 --> 00:13:32.805
Would you hold this for me?
Oh. certainly. sir.

160
00:13:34.679 --> 00:13:37.477
I wonder why he said that.
I beg your pardon?

161
00:13:42.587 --> 00:13:45.317
Captain Ritchie. he said that?
<i>About you? </i>

162
00:13:45.389 --> 00:13:47.152
Oh. repeatedly. sir.

163
00:13:54.031 --> 00:13:57.728
I wonder why he said that.
Thank you.
Oh. thanks.

164
00:13:57.802 --> 00:14:00.703
I wonder if you could get this
over to the crime lab
as soon as possible.

165
00:14:00.771 --> 00:14:03.137
Oh. yes. sir.
This fella have a wife?

166
00:14:03.207 --> 00:14:05.232
Does she know about this?

167
00:14:05.309 --> 00:14:09.678
I suggested they wait until
you had made your preliminary report. sir.
<i>Oh. very good. </i>

168
00:14:09.747 --> 00:14:14.013
Sergeant. I wonder if you could
hang around here and see if you could
locate any more physical evidence.

169
00:14:14.085 --> 00:14:16.144
something that might
do us some good?

170
00:14:16.220 --> 00:14:18.154
<i>Could you do that? </i>
Certainly. sir.

171
00:14:18.222 --> 00:14:20.156
Thank you. Fine.
Lieutenant?

172
00:14:20.224 --> 00:14:22.158
Yes?
Um...

173
00:14:22.226 --> 00:14:26.128
I hope you don't mind Captain Ritchie
assigning me to you like this.

174
00:14:26.197 --> 00:14:29.689
I mean. that is to say I realize
it was done without consulting you. and...

175
00:14:29.767 --> 00:14:33.498
No. Freddie. that's perfectly
all right. Captain Ritchie's
a very fine administrator.

176
00:14:33.571 --> 00:14:36.165
and I'm sure
he just wanted to expose me
to some modern techniques.

177
00:14:36.240 --> 00:14:40.176
No. I appreciate that.
Uh. I think I'll go
the long way around.

178
00:14:40.244 --> 00:14:42.269
Oh. yes. Oh. Lieutenant?

179
00:14:42.346 --> 00:14:44.280
Yes?
Your coat.

180
00:14:44.348 --> 00:14:47.181
Oh. thank you very much.
I'll carry it. Thank you.

181
00:14:52.056 --> 00:14:54.024
<i>[Jarvis]</i>
<i>Well. I must say. Catherine. </i>

182
00:14:54.091 --> 00:14:58.460
our kidnapper. whoever he is.
is certainly no piker.

183
00:14:58.529 --> 00:15:02.829
To demand a ransom
of $300.000.

184
00:15:02.900 --> 00:15:07.564
why. I'll wager there are weeks
here and there even you
don't spend that sort of money.

185
00:15:07.638 --> 00:15:09.799
Don't you ever stop. Jarvis?

186
00:15:09.874 --> 00:15:13.401
However. leaving
our personal affection aside.

187
00:15:13.477 --> 00:15:17.174
you must realize that my situation
is such that even I couldn't pour...

188
00:15:17.248 --> 00:15:20.445
even the smallest drop
into such a huge bucket.

189
00:15:20.518 --> 00:15:23.180
even though I'm not a weakling
with a spendthrift wife.
<i>[Doorbell Chimes]</i>

190
00:15:23.254 --> 00:15:25.245
Oh. shut up. Jarvis.

191
00:15:30.361 --> 00:15:32.295
Uh. Mrs. Goodland?
Yes.

192
00:15:32.363 --> 00:15:34.957
Police department. ma'am.
Lieutenant Columbo.

193
00:15:35.032 --> 00:15:37.933
Yes?
Would you mind
if I came in?

194
00:15:38.002 --> 00:15:42.234
Well. I've already told your people
everything I know. Lieutenant.
in triplicate.

195
00:15:42.306 --> 00:15:44.240
Now. if you'll excuse me.
I have company.

196
00:15:44.308 --> 00:15:47.539
Uh. ma'am. you see. this time.
I've got something to tell you.

197
00:15:47.611 --> 00:15:50.011
Oh.
[Sighs]

198
00:15:50.081 --> 00:15:52.572
Well. come in.

199
00:15:55.653 --> 00:15:59.020
This is Lieutenant. uh...
Columbo.

200
00:15:59.090 --> 00:16:02.082
How do you do. sir?
This is Jarvis Goodland.
Tony's uncle.

201
00:16:02.159 --> 00:16:04.787
Did I hear you say
you have something to tell us?

202
00:16:04.862 --> 00:16:08.764
Uh. yes. sir.
I'm sorry. Mrs. Goodland.

203
00:16:08.833 --> 00:16:11.301
We found your husband's car
about an hour ago.

204
00:16:11.369 --> 00:16:14.964
It was in a canyon
off Middlecross Road.

205
00:16:17.775 --> 00:16:20.039
Smashed up pretty badly.
I'm afraid.

206
00:16:20.111 --> 00:16:23.137
<i>Kind of a long drop</i>
<i>offi that particular spot. </i>

207
00:16:24.215 --> 00:16:28.709
Even worse. we found a bullet hole
in the window on the driver's side.

208
00:16:30.554 --> 00:16:33.921
You already heard this?

209
00:16:36.327 --> 00:16:39.296
- Uh. no.
- <i>Oh. </i>

210
00:16:39.363 --> 00:16:42.423
<i>Well. it kind of seems</i>
<i>to me that if... </i>

211
00:16:42.500 --> 00:16:45.992
somebody popped in and told my wife
that they found my car...

212
00:16:46.070 --> 00:16:48.436
at the bottom of a canyon
with a bullet hole in it.

213
00:16:48.506 --> 00:16:53.409
you know. I think she would
wanna ask if I was in the car.
if I was hurt. if I was alive...

214
00:16:53.477 --> 00:16:57.345
<i>You're quite right. Lieutenant. </i>
<i>We do know much of what</i>
<i>you're telling us. </i>

215
00:16:57.415 --> 00:17:01.681
Jarvis.
It's always better to tell the truth.
my dear. especially to the police.

216
00:17:01.752 --> 00:17:06.086
Jarvis. will you let me handle...

217
00:17:06.157 --> 00:17:10.992
Lieutenant. I received a letter
from Tony. He's perfectly all right.

218
00:17:11.061 --> 00:17:14.428
<i>Really. </i>
How big a ransom did the letter
ask for. ma'am?

219
00:17:14.498 --> 00:17:19.265
- You already knew.
- Oh. no. no. No. uh...
Is that an ashtray?

220
00:17:20.538 --> 00:17:23.666
It's just that letters to wives
and relatives saying
"don't talk to the police."

221
00:17:23.741 --> 00:17:25.675
they often involve a kidnapping.

222
00:17:25.743 --> 00:17:30.305
And I mean. uh.
the way I could just barely
get into the house here.

223
00:17:30.381 --> 00:17:33.316
just now. right here at the door.

224
00:17:33.384 --> 00:17:37.150
well. I make these small observations...
I can't help it. ma'am... sometimes.

225
00:17:37.221 --> 00:17:40.054
- May I see the letter. please?
- Well. you can't.

226
00:17:40.124 --> 00:17:43.685
Aside from the fact it specifically says
not to give the police any information...

227
00:17:43.761 --> 00:17:49.461
<i>Mrs. Goodland. I will do nothing</i>
<i>to endanger the safety of your husband. </i>

228
00:17:49.533 --> 00:17:52.593
But this is a crime.
This is a police matter.

229
00:17:52.670 --> 00:17:56.902
I've already sent it by messenger
to Mr. Jameson at the Golden West Bank.

230
00:17:56.974 --> 00:18:00.375
He's gonna verify Tony's handwriting.
He'll do whatever's necessary.

231
00:18:00.444 --> 00:18:04.005
Catherine. I think you'd better
cooperate more than that.

232
00:18:04.081 --> 00:18:09.246
The letters asked for $300.000
in small unmarked bills.

233
00:18:09.320 --> 00:18:11.481
$300.000?

234
00:18:11.555 --> 00:18:14.683
Well. that's a lot of money.
I mean.

235
00:18:14.758 --> 00:18:18.353
well. do you mind if I ask you.
do you have access...

236
00:18:18.429 --> 00:18:21.887
<i>Well. of course I don't have it. </i>
<i>But Tony has a trust fund. </i>

237
00:18:21.966 --> 00:18:25.959
Now. in an emergency like this...
Ah. the trust fund.

238
00:18:26.036 --> 00:18:28.368
That's why you wanted me here.

239
00:18:28.439 --> 00:18:32.569
Well. Jarvis. I certainly know
you wouldn't help me raise
the money any other way.

240
00:18:32.643 --> 00:18:35.009
I'm sorry. I don't quite understand
about that trust fund.

241
00:18:35.079 --> 00:18:38.173
Well. you see. I am coadministrator
with the bank...

242
00:18:38.249 --> 00:18:40.877
<i>of a trust fund set up</i>
<i>by Tony's father. </i>

243
00:18:40.951 --> 00:18:43.419
And you. Catherine.
should know of all people...

244
00:18:43.487 --> 00:18:47.389
that he put enough strings in there
to protect Tony from his own bad habits...

245
00:18:47.458 --> 00:18:49.449
and grasping wives.

246
00:18:49.527 --> 00:18:53.520
<i>I also know. because Mr. Jameson</i>
<i>told me on the telephone. </i>

247
00:18:53.597 --> 00:18:57.363
that there is an emergency clause
for... well. for problems like this.

248
00:18:57.434 --> 00:19:00.062
- Yes. there is that.
- Then you can get the money?

249
00:19:01.505 --> 00:19:04.736
I mean. you can break the trust fund.
Boy. that's a lucky thing.

250
00:19:04.808 --> 00:19:07.402
We can if the bank
verifies the letter.

251
00:19:07.478 --> 00:19:10.470
<i>[Jarvis]</i>
<i>And if I choose to vote</i>
<i>in Tony's favor. </i>

252
00:19:10.548 --> 00:19:13.312
Now there's no use
glaring at me like that.

253
00:19:13.384 --> 00:19:16.148
Blood is thicker than martinis.

254
00:19:16.220 --> 00:19:19.087
I'll go and seeJameson
right away.
Hmph.

255
00:19:19.156 --> 00:19:23.058
Oh. sir? You will be careful
with the fingerprints. won't you?

256
00:19:23.127 --> 00:19:25.322
I mean. we could help
with the verification.

257
00:19:25.396 --> 00:19:30.925
Why don't I send one of the lab boys
over there to meet you?
Why don't you do that?

258
00:19:31.001 --> 00:19:33.060
Delightful. isn't he?

259
00:19:33.137 --> 00:19:35.571
What? Huh?

260
00:19:35.639 --> 00:19:38.039
Oh. Well.

261
00:19:38.108 --> 00:19:40.372
you know. everybody gets uptight
in a situation like that.

262
00:19:40.444 --> 00:19:43.436
I can understand that.
And. Mrs. Goodland.

263
00:19:43.514 --> 00:19:47.177
believe me. I understand
how concerned you are
about your husband.

264
00:19:47.251 --> 00:19:50.015
And rest assured.
we will do nothing to interfere.

265
00:19:50.087 --> 00:19:53.454
- <i>Just help. </i>
- <i>[Door Opens]</i>

266
00:19:53.524 --> 00:19:56.618
I heard the front door close.
I thought you were alone.

267
00:20:04.034 --> 00:20:06.127
Who are you?

268
00:20:06.203 --> 00:20:09.832
<i>Another cop? </i>
Uh. yes. Lieutenant Columbo.

269
00:20:11.175 --> 00:20:13.837
Ken Nichols.
Friend of the family.

270
00:20:13.911 --> 00:20:16.175
How do you do. sir?

271
00:20:16.246 --> 00:20:19.773
Hey. you look a little tired.

272
00:20:19.850 --> 00:20:23.342
You go on back upstairs
and get some rest.

273
00:20:23.420 --> 00:20:27.516
You let me be the watchdog.
fix him a drink or whatever.

274
00:20:27.591 --> 00:20:30.151
No. he was just leaving.

275
00:20:30.227 --> 00:20:33.253
Uh. yes. I was just leaving.

276
00:20:36.533 --> 00:20:39.798
Now. Mrs. Goodland.
you just follow any instructions
they give you in that letter.

277
00:20:39.870 --> 00:20:42.998
and we'll stay in the background
till your husband's released.

278
00:20:43.073 --> 00:20:46.839
I mean. uh. don't worry.
Everything's gonna be all right.

279
00:20:47.845 --> 00:20:50.507
Lieutenant?
Yes?

280
00:20:50.581 --> 00:20:53.141
I'm scared about Tony.

281
00:20:53.217 --> 00:20:55.344
And I'll do anything on earth
to see him safe.

282
00:20:55.419 --> 00:20:57.819
We lead separate lives.

283
00:20:57.888 --> 00:21:00.823
And I don't really care
what you might be thinking right now.

284
00:21:00.891 --> 00:21:02.882
Good day!

285
00:21:48.372 --> 00:21:50.863
[BellJingling]

286
00:22:02.352 --> 00:22:04.843
<i>[Rustling]</i>

287
00:22:07.891 --> 00:22:09.825
Oh. excuse me.

288
00:22:09.893 --> 00:22:12.487
<i>I hope I didn't startle you. sir. </i>

289
00:22:12.563 --> 00:22:16.727
One of your men...
I believe it was the gardener...
he said it was all right if I waited here.

290
00:22:16.800 --> 00:22:19.701
And I must say.
it's been a real pleasure...

291
00:22:19.770 --> 00:22:23.228
because I've never seen
so many beautiful flowers in my life.

292
00:22:23.307 --> 00:22:25.434
Orchids. Lieutenant.

293
00:22:25.509 --> 00:22:28.945
One of the finest collections
in the country. even if I say so myself.

294
00:22:29.012 --> 00:22:31.310
My wife loves African violets.

295
00:22:31.381 --> 00:22:34.214
but. boy. what a thrill
it would be to her...

296
00:22:34.284 --> 00:22:37.981
I can imagine if I ever brought
something like this home to her...

297
00:22:38.055 --> 00:22:40.523
That specimen happens
to be called a moth orchid.

298
00:22:40.591 --> 00:22:43.685
Its value is
approximately $1200.

299
00:22:43.761 --> 00:22:47.060
$1200. Can you imagine that
for one flower?
Mm-hmm.

300
00:22:47.131 --> 00:22:51.329
Hard to believe. Boy. a fella
could go broke with a hobby like this.
Mm-hmm.

301
00:22:51.401 --> 00:22:54.495
You mean to tell me every one
of these are worth $1200?

302
00:22:54.571 --> 00:22:58.302
<i>Lieutenant Columbo. I enjoy</i>
<i>talking about my orchids. </i>

303
00:22:58.375 --> 00:23:01.936
but I have a feeling you came here
with something else on your mind.

304
00:23:02.012 --> 00:23:05.038
Yes. sir. I'm waiting to hear
how you made out at the bank.

305
00:23:05.115 --> 00:23:07.106
Ah.

306
00:23:08.118 --> 00:23:10.518
And to see this I suppose.

307
00:23:10.587 --> 00:23:14.523
Oh. yes. sir. that's very important.
I'd like to keep that for evidence
if I could.

308
00:23:16.293 --> 00:23:18.727
Let's see if I have
a handkerchief here.

309
00:23:18.796 --> 00:23:21.162
Oh. go ahead!
It won't bite you.

310
00:23:21.231 --> 00:23:24.826
Your expert's already verified
that the fingerprints are Tony's...

311
00:23:24.902 --> 00:23:28.338
<i>and that the handwriting is his. </i>
Oh. he checked it out. did he?

312
00:23:28.405 --> 00:23:31.340
Oh. yes.
Well. then there's no need
to be so careful.

313
00:23:31.408 --> 00:23:33.342
[Coughs]

314
00:23:36.380 --> 00:23:38.348
<i>Let's see. "Cathy. </i>

315
00:23:38.415 --> 00:23:40.440
"there's a man standing over me...

316
00:23:40.517 --> 00:23:43.645
making me write this."

317
00:23:43.720 --> 00:23:46.746
"Driving in a car on a country road.
shot at me."

318
00:23:46.824 --> 00:23:49.759
<i>[Mutters]</i>
<i>"Forced offi the road. "</i>

319
00:23:49.827 --> 00:23:53.558
"Don't worry. I'm not hurt."
That's must have been a relief
when you got to that part.

320
00:23:53.630 --> 00:23:57.157
- Oh. yes. indeed.
- "Demand $300.000.

321
00:23:57.234 --> 00:24:00.226
Whatever you do.
don't tell no police. Sit tight..."

322
00:24:00.304 --> 00:24:03.899
Your expert has told you. I'm sure.
everything including the text.

323
00:24:03.974 --> 00:24:07.034
Yeah. you know.
He did in his way.

324
00:24:07.110 --> 00:24:09.408
And also that the money
will be available.

325
00:24:09.479 --> 00:24:12.243
Yeah. that was a lucky thing.
wasn't it?

326
00:24:12.316 --> 00:24:15.217
And also the fact of your being here
jeopardizes my nephew's life.

327
00:24:15.285 --> 00:24:19.016
<i>Now supposing we were watched. </i>
Good point. sir.

328
00:24:19.089 --> 00:24:21.489
You're absolutely right.

329
00:24:21.558 --> 00:24:24.959
Better run along.
Uh. the. uh...

330
00:24:25.028 --> 00:24:29.192
The one or two little things I have.
I guess they can wait until. uh...

331
00:24:29.266 --> 00:24:31.257
Yeah.

332
00:24:36.373 --> 00:24:38.364
[Sighs]

333
00:24:39.710 --> 00:24:44.147
Now. it just hit me
how much you must love these flowers.

334
00:24:45.215 --> 00:24:47.479
<i>No. when you didn't go</i>
<i>straight to the bank</i>...

335
00:24:47.551 --> 00:24:51.988
I mean. with your nephew being kidnapped.
and they told me you took the time
to stop off at the nursery...

336
00:24:52.055 --> 00:24:55.047
You mean I'm being followed already?

337
00:24:55.125 --> 00:24:58.993
<i>That you're interfering</i>
<i>and you promised you wouldn't? </i>
Uh...

338
00:24:59.062 --> 00:25:02.828
I'm gonna call up
your superiors!
<i>No. there's no need to do that. sir. </i>

339
00:25:02.900 --> 00:25:06.996
No. they've told me.
and they've made it very clear.
I'm to stay in touch.

340
00:25:07.070 --> 00:25:11.302
but until your nephew is released.
believe me. we're way back.

341
00:25:11.375 --> 00:25:14.435
<i>Way back. </i>
<i>Nothing to worry about. </i>

342
00:25:16.847 --> 00:25:21.750
<i>In that case. I don't mind</i>
<i>revealing that my nephew</i>
<i>isn't worth a sack of peat moss. </i>

343
00:25:21.818 --> 00:25:26.255
He's a wife-ridden weakling
whom I've despised for years.

344
00:25:26.323 --> 00:25:29.690
If it wasn't for the fact
that he's my only relative.

345
00:25:29.760 --> 00:25:32.422
I'd call up his captors
and tell them that
they're welcome to him.

346
00:25:39.503 --> 00:25:42.495
<i>[Door Closes]</i>
<i>[Bell Jingles]</i>

347
00:26:35.625 --> 00:26:37.786
Uh. Lieutenant. sir?

348
00:26:39.730 --> 00:26:42.665
The boys on the new shift.
they keep asking me...

349
00:26:42.733 --> 00:26:47.136
why a homicide lieutenant
has requested to stay
on this kidnapping thing. uh...

350
00:26:48.705 --> 00:26:50.935
l... I don't know what
I'm supposed to say.

351
00:26:51.008 --> 00:26:53.408
Are they angry?
I hope they're not angry.
I don't...

352
00:26:53.477 --> 00:26:55.741
Lieutenant. we got a ring.

353
00:26:57.748 --> 00:26:59.739
Oh. Hold that.

354
00:27:04.988 --> 00:27:07.650
[Ringing]

355
00:27:09.860 --> 00:27:11.851
Answer it.

356
00:27:16.066 --> 00:27:18.261
Yes? Tony!

357
00:27:18.335 --> 00:27:20.496
Tony. where are you?

358
00:27:23.173 --> 00:27:25.107
Yes. Jarvis is here.

359
00:27:29.346 --> 00:27:33.646
Yes. I've got the money.
Yes. Tony. I'm listening.

360
00:27:33.717 --> 00:27:37.551
TellJarvis he's to go to...

361
00:27:37.621 --> 00:27:40.181
Cal-Texas Gas Station.

362
00:27:40.257 --> 00:27:44.159
583 5 East Wilshire.

363
00:27:44.227 --> 00:27:46.161
Wait for a call.

364
00:27:46.229 --> 00:27:49.995
[Straining]
Public phone booth.
You got that?

365
00:27:50.067 --> 00:27:52.331
Yes. I've got that.
Tony. are you all right?

366
00:27:52.402 --> 00:27:55.394
Have they hurt you?
You sound so...
[Dial Tone Humming]

367
00:27:57.441 --> 00:27:59.739
They made him hang up.

368
00:28:01.144 --> 00:28:05.672
<i>5835 East Wilshire. </i>
<i>Yes. I think I know the station. </i>

369
00:28:05.749 --> 00:28:07.740
Well. might as well
get it over with.

370
00:28:07.818 --> 00:28:11.845
If you'd just sign this. Mr. Goodland.
Bank rules and all.
Oh. yes. of course.

371
00:28:13.423 --> 00:28:16.654
What about my going
with you. Mr. Goodland?
You?

372
00:28:16.726 --> 00:28:20.423
Sure. I'll hide in the back of the car...
My dear boy.
there's one thing I don't need.

373
00:28:20.497 --> 00:28:22.488
it's a hero.

374
00:28:24.401 --> 00:28:28.269
Now assuming I survive.
I shall telephone and let you know.

375
00:28:45.422 --> 00:28:49.222
Keep him in sight.
No tailgating. understand?
Yes. sir.

376
00:29:40.844 --> 00:29:43.506
<i>[Phone Ringing]</i>

377
00:29:47.651 --> 00:29:50.085
[Line Ringing]

378
00:29:52.455 --> 00:29:55.720
[Line Clicks]
It's about time!

379
00:29:56.860 --> 00:29:59.454
Uh. yeah. yeah.
Okay. okay.

380
00:29:59.529 --> 00:30:03.226
Uh. take Sunset to Surf Road.

381
00:30:03.300 --> 00:30:07.634
North on Surf 4.6 miles.

382
00:30:07.704 --> 00:30:11.105
You got 15 minutes to get there.

383
00:30:41.805 --> 00:30:44.433
[Man]
I think he's stopping. Lieutenant.

384
00:30:44.507 --> 00:30:47.442
[Wilson]
Pull up and turn off the lights.
Yes. sir.

385
00:31:19.042 --> 00:31:21.272
Did you ever see
one of these before. Lieutenant?

386
00:31:21.344 --> 00:31:23.403
Uh...

387
00:31:23.480 --> 00:31:27.075
No. I'm not sure I have.
It. uh. looks kind of
familiar. though.

388
00:31:27.150 --> 00:31:32.247
It's a camera-mounted starlight scope.
They use 'em quite a bit at Berkeley
for night work.

389
00:31:33.323 --> 00:31:35.951
You mean that takes pictures
in the dark?
Yeah.

390
00:31:36.026 --> 00:31:39.792
I bought this one myself.
You used your own money?

391
00:31:39.863 --> 00:31:42.855
Well. I wanted to have
the best equipment for the job. sir.

392
00:31:44.167 --> 00:31:46.158
You must be a bachelor.

393
00:31:49.773 --> 00:31:52.674
<i>[Camera Shutter Clicking]</i>

394
00:33:09.519 --> 00:33:12.784
Lieutenant! We've got some
very clear footprints here.
going and coming.

395
00:33:12.856 --> 00:33:16.292
Good. We'll have some moulage
casts made. I think we better go.

396
00:33:16.359 --> 00:33:19.385
Lieutenant. uh...

397
00:33:19.462 --> 00:33:22.522
I believe I'd rather take
some three-dimension photographs.
if you don't mind.

398
00:33:22.599 --> 00:33:25.159
We've pretty much stopped using
moulage casts. you know.

399
00:33:25.235 --> 00:33:27.635
We have?
<i>Oh. with footprints. </i>
<i>yes. indeed. </i>

400
00:33:27.704 --> 00:33:29.797
<i>You see. we found</i>
<i>that when the plaster swells. </i>

401
00:33:29.873 --> 00:33:33.570
it makes them appear a half
to a full size larger than they really are.

402
00:33:33.643 --> 00:33:36.111
- No kidding?
- Oh. absolutely.

403
00:33:36.179 --> 00:33:38.807
Well. then maybe
we better take pictures.
Oh. very good.

404
00:33:38.882 --> 00:33:42.113
Just as quickly as you can.
Sergeant.
<i>Yes. sir. </i>

405
00:34:27.764 --> 00:34:30.961
Oh. it's you. Columbo.
Yes. sir. I hope
we didn't scare you.

406
00:34:31.034 --> 00:34:34.765
Detective Sergeant Wilson.
You didn't scare me.
but the kidnapper did.

407
00:34:34.838 --> 00:34:37.966
That mask and everything.
frankly. I'm a little unraveled.

408
00:34:38.041 --> 00:34:41.101
Well. that's quite natural.
Mr. Goodland. believe me.
Thank you. young man.

409
00:34:41.177 --> 00:34:45.910
Uh. sir. we're kind of interested in
exactly what happened up there
on that hill.

410
00:34:45.982 --> 00:34:48.780
Well. the man said. "Goodland?"
I said. "Yes."

411
00:34:48.852 --> 00:34:51.548
He said. "Give me the money."
I gave him the money.

412
00:34:51.621 --> 00:34:54.454
<i>I hope you didn't surround</i>
<i>those trees he ran into. </i>

413
00:34:54.524 --> 00:34:58.585
Oh. no. sir. Just as we agreed.
we're gonna stay out of this thing
until your nephew's released.

414
00:34:58.661 --> 00:35:00.993
You wouldn't recognize him again.
would you. if you saw him?

415
00:35:01.064 --> 00:35:04.522
<i>The guy up there in the hill? </i>
I told you.
he had a stocking mask on!

416
00:35:04.601 --> 00:35:06.535
Yeah.

417
00:35:06.603 --> 00:35:09.003
I guess it was pretty dark
up there too.

418
00:35:09.072 --> 00:35:13.270
His voice.
Anything familiar about his voice?
The way he walked maybe?

419
00:35:13.343 --> 00:35:18.007
Lieutenant. I've had a fatiguing
and rather frightening evening.
Can't this wait until tomorrow?

420
00:35:18.081 --> 00:35:23.246
Yeah. I'm sorry. sir.
I guess it must seem to you
that we're not being very considerate.

421
00:35:23.319 --> 00:35:27.722
- Have a pleasant night. sir.
- I presume that's gallows humor.

422
00:35:27.790 --> 00:35:30.122
Good night. young man.

423
00:35:53.049 --> 00:35:56.485
Sorry it was so long. I had to be sure
that Neanderthal policeman
wasn't following us.

424
00:35:56.553 --> 00:35:59.420
[Panting]
Well. it was hairy when
he stopped you. I'll tell you that.

425
00:35:59.489 --> 00:36:01.855
Well. I'll take the bag.
No.

426
00:36:01.925 --> 00:36:03.916
I'll take it.

427
00:36:18.775 --> 00:36:21.266
I've really gotta hand it
to you. UncleJarv.

428
00:36:21.344 --> 00:36:25.906
Unbreakable trust broken
to the tune of 300 thou.

429
00:36:25.982 --> 00:36:29.315
Would you look
at these lovely green bricks.

430
00:36:29.385 --> 00:36:31.319
Beautiful.

431
00:36:31.387 --> 00:36:34.823
Far too beautiful for you to waste
your half on that woman.

432
00:36:34.891 --> 00:36:38.190
That woman happens to be my wife.
and I wanna keep her.

433
00:36:38.261 --> 00:36:40.923
If money's what it takes.
money's what she'll have.

434
00:36:40.997 --> 00:36:43.227
What a waste.

435
00:36:44.500 --> 00:36:46.695
No. Tony. no.

436
00:36:46.769 --> 00:36:50.865
The time has now come for me
to explain to you phase three.

437
00:37:20.003 --> 00:37:22.437
[BellJingling]

438
00:37:25.174 --> 00:37:28.371
Columbo.
Oh. good morning.
Mr. Goodland.

439
00:37:28.444 --> 00:37:32.278
I was hoping I'd find you up.
Uh. your gardener said
I might find you here.

440
00:37:32.348 --> 00:37:34.873
You have something on Tony?
No. sir. No.

441
00:37:34.951 --> 00:37:39.354
I'm afraid we haven't gotten
any kind of report at all.
none at all.

442
00:37:39.422 --> 00:37:41.481
<i>That sounds ominous. </i>

443
00:37:41.557 --> 00:37:44.117
Oh. he could pop up
any minute now. sir.

444
00:37:44.193 --> 00:37:48.630
Of course. uh. there is
that possibility that once
they get him to write the letter...

445
00:37:48.698 --> 00:37:51.258
and make the phone call...
but you never know.

446
00:37:51.334 --> 00:37:55.566
You mean. they may have waited
until the ransom money was paid.
and then...

447
00:37:55.638 --> 00:37:57.697
That's a grisly thought.

448
00:37:57.774 --> 00:38:01.175
Well. you just never know.
but it's good to be positive.

449
00:38:01.244 --> 00:38:05.305
I always like to think positive.
Is that all you came here
to talk to me about?

450
00:38:05.381 --> 00:38:08.179
No. sir. No. I didn't.

451
00:38:08.251 --> 00:38:12.847
Sir. I was hoping that
you'd be able to make
a suggestion.

452
00:38:12.922 --> 00:38:18.554
My wife has tried everything
she knows to get this thing to grow.

453
00:38:18.628 --> 00:38:20.789
This African violet here.

454
00:38:20.863 --> 00:38:26.233
Uh. I was hoping maybe
you'd be able to make a suggestion.

455
00:38:26.302 --> 00:38:29.738
That is the most miserable
specimen I've ever seen.

456
00:38:29.806 --> 00:38:32.536
My only advice to you. Columbo.
is to throw it in the trash can.

457
00:38:34.277 --> 00:38:36.336
Yeah.

458
00:38:37.613 --> 00:38:39.740
I was afraid you were
gonna say that.

459
00:38:39.816 --> 00:38:42.979
Well. what are you gonna do?

460
00:38:43.052 --> 00:38:47.318
Listen. as long as I'm here.
I might as well bring up one or two
little things I didn't get to before.

461
00:38:47.390 --> 00:38:50.382
<i>Uh. your nephew's</i>
<i>red car. for instance. </i>

462
00:38:50.460 --> 00:38:54.658
You know. we found that thing
with the ignition and lights off
and the gear in neutral.

463
00:38:54.731 --> 00:38:59.065
Neutral? But the letter said
he was forced off the road.

464
00:38:59.135 --> 00:39:04.300
Perhaps they grabbed Tony
and pushed the car over the side
to keep it out of sight. don't you think?

465
00:39:04.373 --> 00:39:06.807
Yeah. yeah. Yeah. that's
what it looks like. all right.

466
00:39:06.876 --> 00:39:10.175
Of course. only then.
one of them made that first
telephone call to Mrs. Goodland.

467
00:39:10.246 --> 00:39:13.340
Well. that was to make her
believe the letter when she got it.

468
00:39:13.416 --> 00:39:16.977
She's a very hard woman
to convince of anything.
Lieutenant.

469
00:39:17.053 --> 00:39:20.716
Mm. I wonder how they knew that.

470
00:39:20.790 --> 00:39:24.089
Funny. And no skid marks.

471
00:39:24.160 --> 00:39:27.618
I mean. a really funny...

472
00:39:27.697 --> 00:39:29.790
Say. what is this thing. sir?

473
00:39:29.866 --> 00:39:33.996
That is a multicolored
cattleya bulb from Brazil.

474
00:39:34.070 --> 00:39:36.095
From Brazil? You don't say?
Really?

475
00:39:36.172 --> 00:39:39.335
Skid marks. Lieutenant?
Huh?

476
00:39:39.408 --> 00:39:44.107
- Skid marks?
- Oh. yeah. There were marks
of a heavier car on that road too.

477
00:39:44.180 --> 00:39:46.978
<i>But his Jaguar. you know. boy. </i>
<i>they can really travel. </i>

478
00:39:47.049 --> 00:39:50.018
- I don't know how the heavier
car caught up with him.
- But they took a shot at him.

479
00:39:50.086 --> 00:39:54.147
- Isn't that what he said?
- Yeah. that's what the letter...

480
00:39:54.223 --> 00:39:56.691
Well. you know something.

481
00:39:56.759 --> 00:39:59.353
the line of flight of that bullet
through the window...

482
00:39:59.428 --> 00:40:01.623
Well. that slug would've
passed right through him.

483
00:40:01.697 --> 00:40:03.790
<i>I mean. </i>
<i>ifhe was driving the car. </i>

484
00:40:03.866 --> 00:40:08.360
But it didn't. I mean. nothing.
You know? No blood. nothing.

485
00:40:08.437 --> 00:40:10.564
Just a.3 2-caliber slug
in the seat.

486
00:40:10.640 --> 00:40:14.940
Well. you see.
Tony's been ducking
things adroitly for years.

487
00:40:15.011 --> 00:40:17.411
[Chuckles]
Right. Right.
Uh. very good. sir.

488
00:40:17.480 --> 00:40:19.573
You want this? Here.

489
00:40:19.649 --> 00:40:23.085
Uh. listen. sir.
[Clears Throat]

490
00:40:23.152 --> 00:40:26.519
you've got a gun yourself.
haven't you. Mr. Goodland?

491
00:40:26.589 --> 00:40:28.887
Also a.3 2. I think.

492
00:40:28.958 --> 00:40:31.188
Uh...
Mm-hmm. Uh. yes. yes.

493
00:40:31.260 --> 00:40:33.990
There's one around here somewhere.
I haven't seen it for almost a year.

494
00:40:34.063 --> 00:40:37.032
Uh. Tony gave it to me.
It's around the house somewhere.

495
00:40:37.099 --> 00:40:41.399
Lieutenant.
you been checking up on me?

496
00:40:41.470 --> 00:40:44.735
Oh. no. sir. No. I just happened
to run across a. uh.

497
00:40:44.807 --> 00:40:47.776
police report you filed.
oh. way back there sometime.

498
00:40:47.844 --> 00:40:50.574
<i>Yeah. I had it here a minute ago. </i>
<i>I don't know what happened to it. </i>

499
00:40:50.646 --> 00:40:55.276
Uh. it had to do with somebody
breaking into the. uh...
into the greenhouse here.

500
00:40:55.351 --> 00:40:59.378
- Solarium.
- Oh. "solarium." right.
I stand corrected.

501
00:40:59.455 --> 00:41:02.083
I got this telephone bill.
I gotta take care of that.

502
00:41:02.158 --> 00:41:04.149
Oh. here we are.
Here we are.

503
00:41:04.227 --> 00:41:08.721
Yeah. uh. I guess a guy broke in.
and what happened?
You took some potshots at him.

504
00:41:08.798 --> 00:41:10.857
<i>or something? </i>

505
00:41:10.933 --> 00:41:13.561
Columbo. you're marvelous...

506
00:41:13.636 --> 00:41:15.695
transparent. but marvelous.

507
00:41:15.771 --> 00:41:19.036
You just happened
to run across this report?

508
00:41:19.108 --> 00:41:21.542
Well. uh. it didn't just happen.
I'd forgotten all about it.

509
00:41:21.611 --> 00:41:25.308
I did take a couple of shots.
but all I hit was a pile of dirt
over there.

510
00:41:25.381 --> 00:41:27.872
I scared me
more than I scared the prowler.

511
00:41:27.950 --> 00:41:30.783
Well. you know. with all
the glass you got here.
and the prices the way they are.

512
00:41:30.853 --> 00:41:32.878
it's a good thing you shot low.
believe me.

513
00:41:32.955 --> 00:41:36.721
Well. I confess.
Now I have to change
and get to work.

514
00:41:36.792 --> 00:41:39.488
Confess to what. sir?

515
00:41:39.562 --> 00:41:42.759
To having an unregistered weapon
somewhere in the house.

516
00:41:42.832 --> 00:41:46.563
- That's what you're
leading up to. isn't it?
- Oh. no. sir. Oh. no. not at all.

517
00:41:46.636 --> 00:41:52.074
<i>Listen. if I arrested everybody</i>
<i>with an unregistered weapon</i>
<i>in Los Angeles. </i>

518
00:41:52.141 --> 00:41:54.439
<i>believe me. I'd have half</i>
<i>the population in jail. </i>

519
00:41:54.510 --> 00:41:56.603
Then why are you here.
Columbo?

520
00:41:56.679 --> 00:41:59.273
Oh! Geez!

521
00:41:59.348 --> 00:42:03.079
This is magnificent.
I asked you a question.

522
00:42:03.152 --> 00:42:05.586
I'm sorry. sir. I happen
to love this game.

523
00:42:05.655 --> 00:42:09.523
I played it when I was a kid
and this is such a beautiful table.

524
00:42:09.592 --> 00:42:12.390
I'm sorry. sir.
I didn't mean to hold you up.

525
00:42:12.461 --> 00:42:15.862
You know. in my house.
I don't have room for a table
in my basement...

526
00:42:15.932 --> 00:42:18.025
even if I could afford one.

527
00:42:18.100 --> 00:42:21.297
Uh. I've got these
pictures here. sir.

528
00:42:21.370 --> 00:42:23.838
Uh. these were taken
with a starlight scope.

529
00:42:23.906 --> 00:42:27.433
That's a new camera.
It's a very sophisticated
instrument.

530
00:42:27.510 --> 00:42:29.705
I'd like you to take a look at 'em.

531
00:42:29.779 --> 00:42:35.046
Uh. you know. since you were
right there. Right on the spot.
so to speak.

532
00:42:36.185 --> 00:42:38.380
Where were these pictures
taken from?

533
00:42:38.454 --> 00:42:42.788
Oh. way down at the bottom of the hill.
They don't show very much.
which is kind of funny too.

534
00:42:42.858 --> 00:42:45.884
<i>You don't mind. do you? </i>

535
00:42:45.962 --> 00:42:48.021
What was kind of funny too?

536
00:42:48.097 --> 00:42:50.361
Uh...

537
00:42:50.433 --> 00:42:53.925
Eh. not as rusty
as I thought I was.

538
00:42:54.003 --> 00:42:57.837
Uh. what's funny is that. um.

539
00:42:57.907 --> 00:43:00.740
the place where they asked you
to deliver the ransom.

540
00:43:00.810 --> 00:43:03.904
you know. way up on top
of the hill like that there...

541
00:43:03.980 --> 00:43:07.507
I mean. it's almost as though
they wanted to have a place
that was exposed...

542
00:43:07.583 --> 00:43:10.051
in order to be photographed.

543
00:43:10.119 --> 00:43:12.747
What do you think?
I think it's very odd.

544
00:43:14.123 --> 00:43:18.355
So do I.
I think this whole case is odd.
You know what I mean?

545
00:43:18.427 --> 00:43:21.692
<i>I mean. you got those skid marks</i>
<i>and you got the bullet hole. </i>

546
00:43:21.764 --> 00:43:24.858
I'll tell ya. in most cases.
you don't have any clues.

547
00:43:24.934 --> 00:43:27.368
Gee. I can't miss a shot.

548
00:43:27.436 --> 00:43:30.064
In this case. I got so many clues.
I don't know where to start.

549
00:43:30.139 --> 00:43:33.540
<i>You know. it's almost like</i>
<i>they put 'em there</i>
<i>just on purpose. </i>

550
00:43:33.609 --> 00:43:37.272
You're the detective.
Don't ask me for your answers.

551
00:43:37.346 --> 00:43:40.110
Oh. I can't miss a shot.
Isn't that wonderful?

552
00:43:40.182 --> 00:43:44.312
Um. oh. there is one thing
that I did wanna ask you. sir.

553
00:43:44.387 --> 00:43:47.948
You know what this whole game is?
It's all in the wrist.
You just gotta keep that loose.

554
00:43:48.024 --> 00:43:52.358
Uh. what I wanted to ask you was.
uh. why do you think. uh.

555
00:43:52.428 --> 00:43:55.124
they asked you to deliver the money
instead of the wife?

556
00:43:55.197 --> 00:43:58.394
Because they probably knew
that if Catherine had
that much money in the car.

557
00:43:58.467 --> 00:44:00.458
she'd just keep on driving.

558
00:44:00.536 --> 00:44:03.164
Uh-huh. I wonder how
they knew that.

559
00:44:03.239 --> 00:44:06.231
<i>[Phone Rings]</i>

560
00:44:06.308 --> 00:44:08.367
Yes?

561
00:44:08.444 --> 00:44:10.639
It's for you. Columbo.

562
00:44:10.713 --> 00:44:14.945
Oh! I told them I was gonna be here.
I hope you don't mind. sir.

563
00:44:16.552 --> 00:44:19.020
Hello. Yeah. Columbo.

564
00:44:25.661 --> 00:44:28.425
I'll be there as soon as I can.

565
00:44:30.566 --> 00:44:33.592
- We've got some very bad news. sir.
- What?

566
00:44:33.669 --> 00:44:37.332
They found your nephew's body.
He's been murdered.

567
00:44:40.910 --> 00:44:44.368
[Clears Throat] Yeah.
According to
the coroner's intern.

568
00:44:44.447 --> 00:44:47.712
the bullet. apparently.
went directly through the heart.

569
00:44:47.783 --> 00:44:51.480
fired at extremely close range.
as indicated by the gunpowder traces.

570
00:44:51.554 --> 00:44:53.579
Total envelopment of the body
by rigor mortis.

571
00:44:53.656 --> 00:44:58.059
which is. of course. you know. sir.
fixed to the time of death
at about 10 to 12 hours ago.

572
00:44:58.127 --> 00:45:01.688
The caliber of the bullet
still to be determined.
following the autopsy.

573
00:45:01.764 --> 00:45:05.291
Uh. remove the body. men.
Is that all right with you. sir?

574
00:45:05.367 --> 00:45:07.961
Pronto.
Snap to it. Move it.

575
00:45:09.839 --> 00:45:12.307
Call me soon as you've
got it loaded. I'll come along.

576
00:45:13.476 --> 00:45:17.105
I want that autopsy report
quick as I can get it. sir.

577
00:45:17.179 --> 00:45:19.170
Lieutenant.

578
00:45:19.248 --> 00:45:21.682
Lieutenant. as you've
probably noticed.

579
00:45:21.750 --> 00:45:26.153
there are three cups.
three plates. three different
brands of cigarettes.

580
00:45:26.222 --> 00:45:28.656
That means there were
two persons here
besides the victim.

581
00:45:28.724 --> 00:45:31.716
That's obvious.
Yeah...

582
00:45:31.794 --> 00:45:34.285
Awfully obvious.

583
00:45:36.699 --> 00:45:39.327
<i>[Columbo]</i>
<i>I understand you were</i>
<i>his receptionist for awhile. </i>

584
00:45:39.401 --> 00:45:41.665
Who told you?

585
00:45:41.737 --> 00:45:44.228
Well. his wife sort of mentioned it...
uh. mentioned your name...

586
00:45:44.306 --> 00:45:46.672
Her? I can just imagine.

587
00:45:46.742 --> 00:45:49.040
Strike that from the record.
Oh. sure.

588
00:45:49.111 --> 00:45:51.170
Don't worry about it.
[Sniffles]

589
00:45:51.247 --> 00:45:53.715
<i>That's a good picture of Tony</i>
<i>right there. isn't it? </i>

590
00:45:53.782 --> 00:45:55.773
Oh. I know what you're thinking.

591
00:45:55.851 --> 00:45:59.014
The secret love life
of the murdered man. huh?

592
00:45:59.088 --> 00:46:01.955
[Sniffles]
Well. we sort of like
to contact people who knew him.

593
00:46:02.024 --> 00:46:05.482
regardless in what way.
and I understand that you two
have been acquainted for a good...

594
00:46:05.561 --> 00:46:08.553
Well. you get this straight.
Lieutenant. There was no love affair.

595
00:46:08.631 --> 00:46:10.929
I don't care who told you what.
there just wasn't any.

596
00:46:11.000 --> 00:46:13.525
Well. did you see him?

597
00:46:15.804 --> 00:46:17.999
<i>Miss West. </i>
<i>I'm not here to hurt ya. </i>

598
00:46:18.073 --> 00:46:21.509
And I believe everything you tell me.
I just think you can help me.

599
00:46:21.577 --> 00:46:26.071
<i>and I'd appreciate it</i>
<i>if you would cooperate. </i>

600
00:46:26.148 --> 00:46:28.844
Now. why did he come here
at night?

601
00:46:30.920 --> 00:46:33.115
His wife played around.

602
00:46:34.390 --> 00:46:37.291
So. he'd come here
and he'd tell her so.

603
00:46:37.359 --> 00:46:42.296
Half to try to make her jealous.
and half to show her that...

604
00:46:42.364 --> 00:46:45.458
he didn't really care
that she played around.

605
00:46:45.534 --> 00:46:47.695
Care? He cared. all right.

606
00:46:47.770 --> 00:46:52.139
He'd sit here...
right where you are now... talk.

607
00:46:52.208 --> 00:46:54.608
Did he talk a lot about money?

608
00:46:54.677 --> 00:46:56.702
I mean. lately.
Maybe. uh...

609
00:46:56.779 --> 00:47:01.113
He was always going broke
from his allowance
from some trust thing. I guess.

610
00:47:01.183 --> 00:47:04.152
Did he talk about that...
that trust fund?

611
00:47:04.220 --> 00:47:06.780
[Sighs]
Well. how should I know?

612
00:47:06.855 --> 00:47:10.757
When Tony was drinking...
It's like the other night...

613
00:47:10.826 --> 00:47:12.817
No.

614
00:47:12.895 --> 00:47:16.092
Nope.
What about the other night?

615
00:47:16.165 --> 00:47:19.623
No. I said. Look. Tony's dead now.
Why should people...

616
00:47:19.702 --> 00:47:21.966
Miss West. believe me.

617
00:47:22.037 --> 00:47:24.835
it's a lot better for you
to tell me something now.

618
00:47:24.907 --> 00:47:27.102
then to have to tell it
in front of a jury later on.

619
00:47:27.176 --> 00:47:30.168
In front of what?
I'm not tryin' to scare ya.

620
00:47:30.246 --> 00:47:32.510
and I believe everything
you tell me...

621
00:47:32.581 --> 00:47:35.573
I mean. about the love affair...
I belive everything.

622
00:47:35.651 --> 00:47:38.449
I think you're
a very honest person.

623
00:47:38.520 --> 00:47:40.988
Thanks.
Now. what about
the other night?

624
00:47:42.258 --> 00:47:44.453
[Sighs]

625
00:47:44.526 --> 00:47:49.429
Well. there's this gentleman
that his wife was getting
serious about.

626
00:47:49.498 --> 00:47:54.333
I don't know who.
Tony said he made a living
getting a suntan...

627
00:47:54.403 --> 00:47:56.667
whatever that is.

628
00:47:56.739 --> 00:48:00.505
And then.
about three nights ago.

629
00:48:00.576 --> 00:48:03.204
Tony came in here and he said
everything's gonna be okay...

630
00:48:03.279 --> 00:48:05.372
because...

631
00:48:05.447 --> 00:48:10.407
- Because why?
- Because the gentleman had agreed...

632
00:48:10.486 --> 00:48:14.946
to go away and not to see
Tony's wife ever again if...

633
00:48:16.258 --> 00:48:19.022
<i>if Tony</i>...

634
00:48:19.094 --> 00:48:22.154
<i>if Tony gave him $50.000.</i>

635
00:48:22.231 --> 00:48:25.689
Where was he gonna get the $50.000?
Did he tell you that?
<i>Well. how should I know? </i>

636
00:48:25.768 --> 00:48:28.635
I mean. I was just tryin'
to pour coffee in him.

637
00:48:28.704 --> 00:48:31.036
Honest. sir. I just don't know
any more than that.

638
00:48:31.106 --> 00:48:34.507
Gloria. in your opinion.

639
00:48:34.576 --> 00:48:39.013
was Tony the kind of man
that would arrange
for a fake kidnapping?

640
00:48:39.081 --> 00:48:41.379
Arrange for what?
A fake kidnapping.

641
00:48:41.450 --> 00:48:44.749
To raise the money
in order to break that trust.

642
00:48:44.820 --> 00:48:48.916
Because if he did.
whoever helped him do it
might be the man who killed him.

643
00:48:48.991 --> 00:48:51.721
Oh. look.

644
00:48:51.794 --> 00:48:55.093
l-l-I mean. I said he wasn't
a very strong person.

645
00:48:55.164 --> 00:48:57.155
but then. who is?

646
00:48:57.232 --> 00:48:59.757
I mean. look at me.
I eat carbohydrates all the time.

647
00:49:01.370 --> 00:49:04.032
<i>Please. sir. leave me alone now. </i>

648
00:49:04.106 --> 00:49:06.199
<i>Stop asking me about Tony. </i>

649
00:49:06.275 --> 00:49:10.041
See. I just never met another man
my whole life...

650
00:49:10.112 --> 00:49:12.376
who only wanted to talk.

651
00:49:13.949 --> 00:49:17.112
I understand.
Thank you very much.

652
00:49:47.282 --> 00:49:49.341
[Sniffles]

653
00:49:50.819 --> 00:49:54.516
Hello. sir. Is this you.

654
00:49:54.590 --> 00:49:57.559
Mr. Goodland. to whom I speak?

655
00:50:04.900 --> 00:50:07.994
<i>[Cathy]</i>
<i>I still do not understand you. </i>
<i>Lieutenant. </i>

656
00:50:08.070 --> 00:50:11.506
Just what is it
that you're trying to imply?

657
00:50:11.573 --> 00:50:15.907
Nothing. ma'am.
It's just that you've been
hard to locate at various times.

658
00:50:15.978 --> 00:50:18.139
Uh. oh.

659
00:50:19.348 --> 00:50:21.942
You still don't approve
of my lifestyle. do you?

660
00:50:22.017 --> 00:50:25.578
I told you before.
I really don't care
what you think.

661
00:50:25.654 --> 00:50:29.818
It's about time.
Where'd he come from?

662
00:50:29.892 --> 00:50:33.623
<i>Homicide. of course. </i>
<i>Oh. they handle morals now. </i>

663
00:50:33.695 --> 00:50:37.631
- He's objecting to the places I go.
- No. ma'am. that's not true.

664
00:50:37.699 --> 00:50:41.157
Uh. look. Lieutenant Columbo.
this is. uh...

665
00:50:41.236 --> 00:50:45.468
this is her boat. but it's me
that brought her down here.

666
00:50:45.541 --> 00:50:48.999
Take her away from the house.
give her a change of thoughts.

667
00:50:49.077 --> 00:50:52.638
Well. listen. I think that's
a terrific idea. It's such
a great day for sailing...

668
00:50:52.714 --> 00:50:56.650
<i>I mean. if you like boats. </i>
<i>It's just the night of the murder. </i>

669
00:50:56.718 --> 00:50:59.551
- That's all I wanna ask about.
- Well. what about it. Lieutenant?

670
00:50:59.621 --> 00:51:02.454
Well. sir. uh...
What's your first name?

671
00:51:02.524 --> 00:51:05.755
- Ken.
- Ken. we have a very efficient officer.

672
00:51:05.828 --> 00:51:08.797
His name is Freddie Wilson.
and he happened to report...

673
00:51:08.864 --> 00:51:12.163
that Mrs. Goodland's car
was gone from the house...

674
00:51:12.234 --> 00:51:15.362
about the same time
that her husband was killed.

675
00:51:15.437 --> 00:51:18.565
So. you came down here
to accuse me of murder?
<i>No. ma'am. </i>

676
00:51:18.640 --> 00:51:21.734
It's only that...

677
00:51:21.810 --> 00:51:25.075
Well. you see. something new
has come up and. uh.

678
00:51:25.147 --> 00:51:27.240
I have to get rid
of all these little things first.

679
00:51:27.316 --> 00:51:30.308
I was out... with Ken.

680
00:51:30.385 --> 00:51:32.478
We took a nice. long drive...

681
00:51:32.554 --> 00:51:35.045
<i>and you can make</i>
<i>whatever you like out of that. </i>

682
00:51:35.123 --> 00:51:39.583
My worry for Tony did not require
my staying around the house
until his return...

683
00:51:39.661 --> 00:51:41.993
on pins or needles.

684
00:51:42.064 --> 00:51:44.225
Yes. ma'am. Yes.
I mean. I figured that.

685
00:51:44.299 --> 00:51:47.427
<i>You know something. </i>
<i>Mrs. Goodland? </i>

686
00:51:49.538 --> 00:51:52.371
You're a very unusual person.

687
00:51:52.441 --> 00:51:54.500
You're not a hypocrite.

688
00:51:54.576 --> 00:51:58.205
and I'm not gonna bother you
anymore with these things.

689
00:52:01.617 --> 00:52:04.916
Okay. Charlie. let's cast off.

690
00:52:04.987 --> 00:52:07.046
Oh. there's one little thing. um...

691
00:52:07.122 --> 00:52:10.580
<i>You know. this is gonna sound</i>
<i>kind of silly. I guess. </i>

692
00:52:10.659 --> 00:52:12.684
Take it for what it's worth.

693
00:52:12.761 --> 00:52:17.130
You see. somebody tried to convince me
that you had a lover. Mrs. Goodland.

694
00:52:17.199 --> 00:52:22.432
<i>Not only that. this person. </i>
<i>Gloria West</i>... <i>Young girl. </i>
<i>that was her name. Gloria West. </i>

695
00:52:22.504 --> 00:52:25.302
Anyway. she said that. uh.
this mysterious lover of yours.

696
00:52:25.374 --> 00:52:27.672
some guy with a deep suntan.

697
00:52:27.743 --> 00:52:31.201
that he'd go away and get out
of your life forever...

698
00:52:31.280 --> 00:52:33.475
if your husband gave him
$50.000.

699
00:52:34.550 --> 00:52:37.144
<i>I'm sure it's just</i>
<i>malicious gossip. </i>

700
00:52:37.219 --> 00:52:39.278
<i>I probably shouldn't</i>
<i>have mentioned it. </i>

701
00:52:39.354 --> 00:52:42.323
However.

702
00:52:42.391 --> 00:52:44.382
for what it's worth.

703
00:53:13.121 --> 00:53:15.248
<i>[Doorbell Chimes]</i>

704
00:53:39.915 --> 00:53:42.110
[BellJingling]

705
00:53:46.688 --> 00:53:49.122
[BellJingling]

706
00:53:49.191 --> 00:53:51.250
Mr. Goodland.

707
00:53:57.599 --> 00:54:00.693
<i>[Ringing]</i>

708
00:54:06.708 --> 00:54:09.973
Mr. Goodland.
<i>Ah. Miss West. </i>

709
00:54:10.045 --> 00:54:12.138
I'm sorry I couldn't
meet you sooner.

710
00:54:12.214 --> 00:54:14.273
You said you wanted
to speak to me alone.

711
00:54:14.349 --> 00:54:17.182
Yes. sir. It's a...
It's... Oh.

712
00:54:17.252 --> 00:54:19.743
Gee. it's kind of spooky
in here. isn't it?

713
00:54:19.821 --> 00:54:23.313
You don't like orchids?
Oh. really.
they're my favorite corsage.

714
00:54:23.392 --> 00:54:28.329
Indeed! You said something
on the phone about seeing
Tony the other night.

715
00:54:28.397 --> 00:54:31.423
Yes. sir. and since
you're his relative...

716
00:54:31.500 --> 00:54:34.298
and you've been so polite
the couple of times we've met...

717
00:54:34.369 --> 00:54:37.998
Anyway. this detective
came to call this afternoon.
Oh.

718
00:54:38.073 --> 00:54:40.598
Rumpled raincoat?
Rumpled face?
That's him.

719
00:54:40.676 --> 00:54:42.667
A lieutenant!

720
00:54:42.744 --> 00:54:45.269
Of course. I didn't
tell him everything...

721
00:54:45.347 --> 00:54:47.406
about Tony and me.
I mean.

722
00:54:47.482 --> 00:54:50.212
And some of it I didn't
even think of until later.

723
00:54:50.285 --> 00:54:55.154
- Some of what. Miss West?
- Well. I think that...

724
00:54:55.223 --> 00:54:58.522
he thinks that maybe
Tony's kidnapping...

725
00:54:58.593 --> 00:55:00.959
wasn't a real kidnapping at all.

726
00:55:01.029 --> 00:55:04.362
I beg your pardon?
Like. maybe. Tony did it himself...

727
00:55:04.433 --> 00:55:06.526
to try to get some money
out of his trust fund.

728
00:55:06.601 --> 00:55:09.593
And. as a matter of fact.
Tony did mention to me...

729
00:55:09.671 --> 00:55:12.538
that he might be able
to get me a new car pretty soon.

730
00:55:12.607 --> 00:55:15.007
And you believed his usual
drunken promises?

731
00:55:15.077 --> 00:55:17.602
Uh. well. no.
not really. I guess.

732
00:55:17.679 --> 00:55:20.341
Tell me more
about Columbo's little theory.

733
00:55:20.415 --> 00:55:23.475
I suppose my nephew
also murdered himself.

734
00:55:23.552 --> 00:55:26.817
No! That was whoever
helped Tony. I guess.

735
00:55:26.888 --> 00:55:29.584
and now that person has got
all that ransom money too.

736
00:55:29.658 --> 00:55:32.126
Mm. it sounds quite absurd to me.

737
00:55:32.194 --> 00:55:34.822
Tell me. why did you come to me
with all this nonsense?

738
00:55:34.896 --> 00:55:39.492
Oh. but it's not. maybe.
because I also remembered...

739
00:55:39.568 --> 00:55:42.594
Well. a long time ago...
Oh. gosh. over a year ago...

740
00:55:42.671 --> 00:55:47.108
Tony told me...
Well. see. on the radio
I heard that Tony was killed...

741
00:55:47.175 --> 00:55:50.633
by a bullet
from a.3 2-caliber gun.

742
00:55:50.712 --> 00:55:53.840
Yes?
Well. a long time ago.
like I said.

743
00:55:53.915 --> 00:55:57.851
Tony told me he had a.3 2
that he'd given away.

744
00:55:57.919 --> 00:56:01.411
and I remember now
who he told me he gave it to.

745
00:56:01.490 --> 00:56:06.189
And who was that. Miss West?
<i>His wife. </i>

746
00:56:06.261 --> 00:56:08.752
Well. don't you see
how that fits?

747
00:56:08.830 --> 00:56:11.355
Maybe she and Tony
planned the kidnapping together.

748
00:56:11.433 --> 00:56:16.166
<i>I bet she never even got</i>
<i>that threatening phone call</i>
<i>she told the police about. </i>

749
00:56:16.238 --> 00:56:20.334
So. after the ransom was paid.
she brought in her boyfriend
and killed him...

750
00:56:20.408 --> 00:56:22.467
Uh. Tony. I mean.
not the boyfriend.

751
00:56:22.544 --> 00:56:25.240
And so they split the ransom
and she gets the estate...

752
00:56:25.313 --> 00:56:27.611
and nobody's the wiser.
except me.

753
00:56:27.682 --> 00:56:31.618
And. now. me.
But why me rather
than the police?

754
00:56:31.686 --> 00:56:34.678
Oh. I don't know.
I always feel funny
around policemen.

755
00:56:34.756 --> 00:56:37.589
And. anyway. it's you who's
in charge ofTony's trust. isn't it?

756
00:56:37.659 --> 00:56:40.093
In conjunction with the bank.
yes.

757
00:56:40.162 --> 00:56:42.926
Well. the radio says
there will be a reward...

758
00:56:42.998 --> 00:56:45.558
for whoever gets
that ransom money back...

759
00:56:45.634 --> 00:56:48.762
$30.000 reward...
and I'm claiming it.

760
00:56:48.837 --> 00:56:53.706
I'm gonna help put that
woman in prison and get paid
$30.000 for it too.

761
00:56:53.775 --> 00:56:57.404
I'm sure you will. my dear.
And you're quite right
about the police.

762
00:56:57.479 --> 00:56:59.879
especially that stupid lieutenant.

763
00:56:59.948 --> 00:57:02.314
Now. why don't you let me
handle things for awhile. hmm?

764
00:57:02.384 --> 00:57:05.080
Oh. well. but you won't
forget about me. will ya?

765
00:57:05.153 --> 00:57:07.587
I mean. the reward.
Miss West.
I'll never forget you.

766
00:57:07.656 --> 00:57:10.352
Now. you just run along
while I make some phone calls.

767
00:57:10.425 --> 00:57:13.724
and when the time comes
for you to give your information
to the proper authorities.

768
00:57:13.795 --> 00:57:16.696
I'll be in touch.
Thank you.

769
00:58:01.943 --> 00:58:04.241
<i>[Sheets Rustling]</i>

770
00:59:31.766 --> 00:59:34.030
[Sighs]

771
00:59:34.102 --> 00:59:37.333
<i>[Sirens Wailing In Distance]</i>

772
00:59:38.707 --> 00:59:41.699
<i>[Sirens Approaching]</i>

773
00:59:48.116 --> 00:59:50.175
<i>[Car Door Closes]</i>

774
00:59:51.853 --> 00:59:56.313
- [BellJingling]
- Mr. Goodland. sir.
I came over as quickly as I could.

775
00:59:56.391 --> 00:59:59.019
As soon as I received your message.
Thank you. Sergeant.
Thank you.

776
00:59:59.094 --> 01:00:01.358
I heard your sirens
from quite a ways off.

777
01:00:01.429 --> 01:00:05.923
Now. I would appreciate it
if you would hand this gun
to your ballistics experts.

778
01:00:06.001 --> 01:00:08.196
I rummaged around for quite
some time this evening.

779
01:00:08.269 --> 01:00:11.466
and I finally found it
in a wall safe in my bedroom.

780
01:00:11.539 --> 01:00:14.372
Uh. I don't understand.
Well. you see.

781
01:00:14.442 --> 01:00:17.138
when I told your
Lieutenant Columbo...

782
01:00:17.212 --> 01:00:20.670
that I'd owned a.3 2. but I hadn't
seen it for several months.

783
01:00:20.749 --> 01:00:25.448
he immediately leapt to accusations
that that possibly could be the gun
that killed my nephew.

784
01:00:25.520 --> 01:00:28.421
<i>Now. I resent that implication. </i>
<i>Sergeant. </i>

785
01:00:29.624 --> 01:00:31.615
Well. sir.

786
01:00:31.693 --> 01:00:35.789
different officers do have
their different methods.

787
01:00:35.864 --> 01:00:40.426
I must say. the lieutenant's
investigatory procedures do differ
somewhat from my own.

788
01:00:40.502 --> 01:00:43.903
Well. that speaks very well
for you. Sergeant Wilson.
Well. thank you very much.

789
01:00:43.972 --> 01:00:48.671
Now. I've heard things which cast
an entirely different light
on my nephew's death.

790
01:00:48.743 --> 01:00:52.406
Things so incredible
I can hardly believe them.

791
01:00:52.480 --> 01:00:54.812
Let's go into the house.
shall we?

792
01:00:54.883 --> 01:00:58.148
Now. I feel it my duty to...

793
01:00:58.219 --> 01:01:00.551
tell these things as I see them.

794
01:01:06.161 --> 01:01:09.221
How do you want your chili.
Lieutenant. with or without beans?

795
01:01:10.465 --> 01:01:12.490
Last night I had it with beans?
Right.

796
01:01:12.567 --> 01:01:15.536
Have it without beans...
variety.
All right.

797
01:01:16.771 --> 01:01:20.867
Lieutenant.
what are you doing here?
Just ordering some chili.

798
01:01:22.343 --> 01:01:24.368
Would you excuse us. please?

799
01:01:24.446 --> 01:01:28.940
Sir. didn't you get my report
on theJarvis Goodland statement?

800
01:01:29.017 --> 01:01:31.645
Yes. I found that
very interesting.

801
01:01:31.719 --> 01:01:34.586
Very interesting.
That gun he gave you.

802
01:01:34.656 --> 01:01:36.647
checked out okay
with Ballistics. huh?

803
01:01:36.724 --> 01:01:38.954
Sure. Of course.

804
01:01:39.027 --> 01:01:41.791
Sir. uh. he's cracked
the case for us.

805
01:01:41.863 --> 01:01:44.457
I have a search warrant
and two units right here
ready to go.

806
01:01:44.532 --> 01:01:48.263
If we turn Catherine Goodland's
place upside down. I guarantee you
we'll find that murder weapon.

807
01:01:48.336 --> 01:01:50.668
We'll find it.
You really think so?

808
01:01:50.738 --> 01:01:53.969
Well. unless she's already
gotten rid of it.
Tell you what.

809
01:01:54.042 --> 01:01:56.033
You go ahead.

810
01:01:56.111 --> 01:01:59.171
Go ahead on your own.
You find anything.
you let me know.

811
01:01:59.247 --> 01:02:02.978
Well. sir. if you don't mind
my taking charge for a moment.
Not at all.

812
01:02:03.051 --> 01:02:05.349
Thank you. sir.
Good luck to you.

813
01:02:05.420 --> 01:02:08.912
Charlie. pull 'em out!
[Engines Starting]

814
01:02:08.990 --> 01:02:12.016
Who's that?
Wilson?

815
01:02:12.093 --> 01:02:15.358
Oh. very nice fella.

816
01:02:15.430 --> 01:02:18.922
Been a big help to me
on this case.

817
01:02:26.508 --> 01:02:30.968
<i>[Voices On Police Radio. </i>
<i>Indistinct]</i>

818
01:02:31.045 --> 01:02:33.980
You needn't have bothered
about a search warrant. Sergeant.

819
01:02:34.048 --> 01:02:36.312
All you had to do was to ask.

820
01:02:36.384 --> 01:02:39.785
The pistol's right here
where I always keep it.

821
01:02:39.854 --> 01:02:43.449
Would you take it out
for us. please?
[Chuckles]

822
01:02:47.562 --> 01:02:50.087
Well. it isn't here.

823
01:02:50.165 --> 01:02:52.326
I can see that.

824
01:02:54.269 --> 01:02:56.533
Well. this can't be.

825
01:02:56.604 --> 01:02:59.198
I saw it last night and I haven't
opened this drawer since then.

826
01:02:59.274 --> 01:03:01.504
What's this all about. Sergeant?

827
01:03:01.576 --> 01:03:03.601
The murder of your husband.
Mrs. Goodland.

828
01:03:05.413 --> 01:03:07.540
Grover. bring in the troops.

829
01:03:21.596 --> 01:03:24.895
<i>[Beeping]</i>

830
01:03:39.814 --> 01:03:42.078
Jarvis. what do you want?

831
01:03:42.150 --> 01:03:45.119
I was concerned about you.
my dear.

832
01:03:46.354 --> 01:03:49.983
Have you called your lawyer?
<i>[Wilson]</i>
<i>Mrs. Goodland? </i>

833
01:03:50.058 --> 01:03:54.051
Oh. I'm glad to see
that you're here.
She may need someone.

834
01:03:56.064 --> 01:03:58.362
Mrs. Goodland.
you recognize this?

835
01:03:58.433 --> 01:04:00.993
Well. yes. it was Tony's.

836
01:04:01.069 --> 01:04:03.731
- And this?
- Tony's.

837
01:04:07.942 --> 01:04:10.934
And how about this?
The ransom bag.

838
01:04:11.012 --> 01:04:13.537
Well. it certainly looks like it.
Good heavens. Cathy.

839
01:04:13.615 --> 01:04:17.551
- I don't get it.
- Well. it was under a pile
of Christmas decorations...

840
01:04:17.619 --> 01:04:19.712
in the storage closet.

841
01:04:19.787 --> 01:04:22.585
<i>Mrs. Goodland. I think</i>
<i>it's my duty to inform you</i>...
<i>Nowjust a moment.! </i>

842
01:04:22.657 --> 01:04:25.888
In all fairness to the lady.
when I said that looked like
the ransom bag.

843
01:04:25.960 --> 01:04:28.394
that didn't mean I could
positively identify it.

844
01:04:28.463 --> 01:04:31.432
It's a very common type.
But. sir. it answers the description
in every particular...

845
01:04:31.499 --> 01:04:34.229
- Nevertheless. we must be sure.
- We?

846
01:04:35.703 --> 01:04:39.537
Sir. if there's anything else
here at all. I'll find it.

847
01:04:39.607 --> 01:04:42.872
Grover. back upstairs.

848
01:04:42.944 --> 01:04:44.935
Excuse me.

849
01:04:48.816 --> 01:04:51.011
[Beeping]

850
01:04:51.085 --> 01:04:53.952
<i>Sergeant. for my money. </i>
<i>that pistol is long gone. </i>

851
01:04:54.022 --> 01:04:56.752
Grover. you and I know that
a pro drops the gun immediately.

852
01:04:56.824 --> 01:04:58.815
but we're dealing with amateurs.

853
01:04:58.893 --> 01:05:01.919
I'm guessing that
they're gonna hide the gun
somewhere close by.

854
01:05:01.996 --> 01:05:04.590
Nothing.
Nothing. Nothing.

855
01:05:05.900 --> 01:05:08.425
What about this area over here.
Did you go over this?

856
01:05:08.503 --> 01:05:11.165
We've been through it
twice already. Sergeant.
Well. go over it again.

857
01:05:11.239 --> 01:05:13.901
[Beeping]
<i>Come on. Let's go. </i>

858
01:05:15.343 --> 01:05:18.369
[Beeping Rapidly]
What's that?

859
01:05:18.446 --> 01:05:21.973
Shoes with metal trees
in them. Sergeant.
That's all.

860
01:05:22.050 --> 01:05:24.883
That's what's making
the buzzing.
Okay.

861
01:05:24.952 --> 01:05:27.614
Look. there's a linen closet
out in the hall.
Go check over that.

862
01:05:29.490 --> 01:05:33.790
- Wait a minute.
Did you open all of these?
- <i>No. sir. there was no point in it. </i>

863
01:05:33.861 --> 01:05:36.489
Well. let's open them.

864
01:05:43.504 --> 01:05:45.768
Hold it.

865
01:05:47.308 --> 01:05:49.401
Hmm.
[Chuckles]

866
01:05:52.313 --> 01:05:54.372
Grover.

867
01:05:57.251 --> 01:06:01.620
Crime lab. Pronto. Have Ballistics
check the pistol against the two bullets
they've got. then call me. understand?

868
01:06:01.689 --> 01:06:04.658
Don't you want me to check
with Lieutenant Columbo?
I'm in charge here. Grover.

869
01:06:04.726 --> 01:06:08.184
If that's the murder weapon.
I'll take Mrs. Goodland into custody.
Step on it.

870
01:06:08.262 --> 01:06:10.753
[Slaps Back]
[Mouths Words]

871
01:07:07.021 --> 01:07:09.683
<i>[Crashing]</i>

872
01:07:10.992 --> 01:07:13.085
<i>[Rattling]</i>

873
01:07:19.434 --> 01:07:21.868
<i>What the devil</i>
<i>are you doing here? </i>

874
01:07:21.936 --> 01:07:24.803
Oh. just sort of killing time.
looking around.

875
01:07:24.872 --> 01:07:30.310
You know. sir. I could...
I could turn into a real orchid fancier
since I met you.

876
01:07:30.378 --> 01:07:32.869
Will you tell me
what you're doing here?

877
01:07:32.947 --> 01:07:35.780
It's very serious. sir.

878
01:07:35.850 --> 01:07:38.318
There's been a new
development in the case.
<i>Yes. I know. </i>

879
01:07:38.386 --> 01:07:41.913
They found the murder weapon
in Cathy's house.
I just came from there.

880
01:07:41.989 --> 01:07:45.254
Things certainly
look bad for her.
They certainly do. sir.

881
01:07:45.326 --> 01:07:47.317
That's why I'm waiting here
for the lab report.

882
01:07:47.395 --> 01:07:49.386
I'm hoping to straighten
a few things out.

883
01:07:49.464 --> 01:07:52.729
Look. it's 3:00 in the morning.
Lieutenant. Will you tell me
what you're doing here?

884
01:07:52.800 --> 01:07:57.100
I bumped over this empty pot
and displaced some of the soil here.
I'm sorry about the mess. sir.

885
01:07:57.171 --> 01:08:00.265
- I'll see to it that it gets cleaned up.
- Look. forget that!

886
01:08:00.341 --> 01:08:03.037
Will you tell me why you're here?

887
01:08:03.110 --> 01:08:08.275
To tell you the truth. sir.
I didn't expect you back so soon.

888
01:08:08.349 --> 01:08:10.408
Oh!

889
01:08:10.485 --> 01:08:12.578
Don't wanna forget this.

890
01:08:12.653 --> 01:08:15.645
- You have a real green thumb. sir.
- I what?

891
01:08:16.891 --> 01:08:19.052
This African violet of my wife's.

892
01:08:19.126 --> 01:08:21.219
you know there's actually
a flower growing out of there.

893
01:08:21.295 --> 01:08:25.288
Now. I don't know what you did.
but whatever it was. that's a miracle.

894
01:08:25.366 --> 01:08:27.732
<i>Lieutenant. it's been</i>
<i>a trying evening... </i>

895
01:08:27.802 --> 01:08:29.793
and I'm quite distressed.

896
01:08:29.871 --> 01:08:32.362
Now. will you please take
your African violet
and get out of here!

897
01:08:32.440 --> 01:08:34.965
<i>[Car Approaching]</i>
Wait a minute.
I hear something.

898
01:08:35.042 --> 01:08:37.101
<i>[Car Door Opens]</i>

899
01:08:37.178 --> 01:08:39.510
That could be the man
I'm waiting for.

900
01:08:39.580 --> 01:08:41.639
Grover!

901
01:08:41.716 --> 01:08:45.049
<i>Grover. is that you? </i>
Lieutenant. I don't understand.

902
01:08:45.119 --> 01:08:48.953
I was halfway downtown
with Mrs. Goodland
when we were ordered back here.

903
01:08:49.023 --> 01:08:51.685
<i>I'm sorry. Sergeant. </i>
<i>I didn't mean to run you</i>
<i>around town like that. </i>

904
01:08:51.759 --> 01:08:54.057
Mrs. Goodland. how are you?
You must be exhausted.

905
01:08:54.128 --> 01:08:57.256
Would you like to sit down?
No. No. I'll stand.
Thank you.

906
01:08:57.331 --> 01:08:59.492
Uh. let me get you a chair.

907
01:08:59.567 --> 01:09:03.196
You'll be more comfortable.
I know you've been up all night.

908
01:09:04.272 --> 01:09:07.639
Well. I think they'll be
plenty of time to rest in jail.
don't you?

909
01:09:08.843 --> 01:09:11.573
Sergeant. has this lady
actually been arrested?

910
01:09:11.646 --> 01:09:14.843
Well. l. uh... Sir. I phoned my report
into Captain Ritchie.

911
01:09:14.916 --> 01:09:18.249
He was quite complimentary.
She'll be charged. as soon as we...

912
01:09:18.319 --> 01:09:21.482
No. Sergeant.
No. Mrs. Goodland...

913
01:09:21.556 --> 01:09:23.547
Damn it. Columbo!
What's this all about?

914
01:09:23.624 --> 01:09:27.890
Well. you see. sir. I'm waiting here
for some things from Headquarters.
If you'll all just bear with me.

915
01:09:27.962 --> 01:09:30.522
What sort of things?
<i>[Grover]</i>
<i>Lieutenant.! </i>

916
01:09:30.598 --> 01:09:33.431
- <i>Lieutenant Columbo.! </i>
- Oh.

917
01:09:38.172 --> 01:09:42.074
Oh. Here you are. Lieutenant.
Thank you. Thank you very much.

918
01:09:50.818 --> 01:09:52.911
Excuse me for just a moment.

919
01:10:01.762 --> 01:10:05.596
Yes. I have some bullets here.

920
01:10:05.666 --> 01:10:07.725
This one is from the wrecked car.

921
01:10:07.802 --> 01:10:10.202
A.3 2-caliber. proven by Ballistics...

922
01:10:10.271 --> 01:10:12.466
<i>to have been fired</i>
<i>from the murder weapon. </i>

923
01:10:12.540 --> 01:10:15.065
This one is from the body
of the victim.

924
01:10:15.142 --> 01:10:18.509
also.3 2-caliber.
and proven by Ballistics...

925
01:10:18.579 --> 01:10:21.275
to have been fired
from the same weapon
as the first bullet.

926
01:10:21.349 --> 01:10:24.546
We know all about that.
Tell him. young man.

927
01:10:24.619 --> 01:10:28.851
Both... Both of those
came from the gun
that was found in her house.

928
01:10:28.923 --> 01:10:32.120
And Sergeant Grover
said they confirmed it
as the murder weapon.

929
01:10:32.193 --> 01:10:35.720
<i>Right. That's quite right. </i>

930
01:10:35.796 --> 01:10:38.196
Sergeant. I don't want you
to feel badly.

931
01:10:38.265 --> 01:10:40.563
because without you.
I'd never have gotten this idea.

932
01:10:40.635 --> 01:10:43.900
<i>I mean. those technical things</i>
<i>that you're so good at. </i>

933
01:10:43.971 --> 01:10:46.132
You see.

934
01:10:46.207 --> 01:10:49.040
I've never used
a metal detector before.

935
01:10:49.110 --> 01:10:51.601
That's why it took me
nearly an hour.

936
01:10:51.679 --> 01:10:53.840
<i>But. you know. </i>
<i>these things really work. </i>

937
01:10:55.516 --> 01:10:57.677
Amazing.

938
01:11:02.423 --> 01:11:04.414
You see that?

939
01:11:04.492 --> 01:11:07.655
- What is it?
- Third bullet.

940
01:11:07.728 --> 01:11:12.165
<i>Also a.3 2</i>-<i>caliber. </i>
<i>and also proven by Ballistics... </i>

941
01:11:12.233 --> 01:11:16.533
to have been fired
by the same weapon...

942
01:11:16.604 --> 01:11:19.300
that fired the first two bullets.

943
01:11:19.373 --> 01:11:22.865
Mr. Goodland. I just don't know
how you're gonna explain this.

944
01:11:24.211 --> 01:11:26.145
But why should I have to...

945
01:11:27.948 --> 01:11:30.007
<i>That's right. </i>

946
01:11:30.084 --> 01:11:33.815
That's right. sir.
That's what I was doing over there
a little while ago.

947
01:11:33.888 --> 01:11:35.913
I found this third bullet...

948
01:11:35.990 --> 01:11:38.049
buried here in this pile of dirt.

949
01:11:40.061 --> 01:11:44.157
I guess it was one of those bullets
that you fired at that guy
who broke in here a year ago.

950
01:11:44.231 --> 01:11:46.495
You said you only hit dirt.

951
01:11:46.567 --> 01:11:48.865
I don't know
how you're gonna explain. sir.

952
01:11:48.936 --> 01:11:54.033
how the same gun that fired
this bullet in the dirt.

953
01:11:54.108 --> 01:11:57.077
ended up tonight
in Mrs. Goodland's dressing room.

954
01:11:59.613 --> 01:12:04.209
Sergeant. would you take
Mr. Goodland downtown. please?

955
01:12:07.188 --> 01:12:11.921
Mr. Jarvis Goodland.
it's my duty to inform you
that anything you... you might...

956
01:12:11.992 --> 01:12:13.983
This way sir.

957
01:12:28.743 --> 01:12:30.870
[Sighs]

958
01:12:37.585 --> 01:12:42.249
Mrs. Goodland.
would you allow me
to drive you home?

959
01:12:42.323 --> 01:12:45.520
[Laughs]
Thank you. Lieutenant.

960
01:12:47.895 --> 01:12:50.625
Oh! One moment.

961
01:12:56.971 --> 01:12:59.371
If I forget this.
my wife will kill me.

962
01:13:00.305 --> 01:14:00.902
Tired of searching for subtitles?
Ray generates them instantly: getray.app
